"- button\n- button\n- button\n- tablist:\n  - tab [selected]:\n    - generic: Echo\n  - tab:\n- button [expanded]:\n- button:\n  - generic: 新建任务\n- list:\n  - link:\n    - /url: \"#/workspace/agents?surface=chat\"\n    - generic: HUB\n  - link:\n    - /url: \"#/workspace/realtime/octopus-assistant?agent=octopus\"\n    - generic: 助手\n  - link:\n    - /url: \"#/workspace/intelligence?surface=chat\"\n    - generic: 订阅\n  - link:\n    - /url: \"#/workspace/projects\"\n    - generic: 项目管理\n  - link:\n    - /url: \"#/workspace/design\"\n    - generic: 设计画布\n  - link:\n    - /url: \"#/workspace/narrative\"\n    - generic: 叙事工坊\n  - link:\n    - /url: \"#/workspace/evolution?surface=chat\"\n    - generic: 自进化\n- list:\n  - link:\n    - /url: \"#/workspace/community\"\n    - generic: 发现社区\n- list:\n  - button:\n    - generic: 本地数据库\n- list:\n  - button:\n- button [expanded]:\n  - generic: 项目\n- button:\n- button:\n  - generic: live-codex-workspace\n  - generic: \"5\"\n- button:\n- button [expanded]:\n  - generic: 对话\n- button:\n- list:\n  - link:\n    - /url: \"#/workspace/realtime/tVzjQc51k71eLx8xYMQu1j\"\n    - generic: 研究eight sleep专利布局方向\n    - generic: 1h\n  - button:\n  - link:\n    - /url: \"#/workspace/realtime/tnwquwTzTuEqf3gj5PD4hm\"\n    - generic: 调研智能睡眠\n    - generic: 6h\n  - button:\n- button:\n  - generic: Eve\n- button:\n- main\n- region \"Notifications alt+T\"\n- dialog:\n  - heading [level=2]: Zero\n  - paragraph: ARM / Skill 白名单 / 权限范围 / Runtime\n  - button:\n  - generic: CHARACTER FILE\n  - button:\n  - generic: 角色档案\n  - heading [level=1]: Zero\n  - paragraph: 现场执行官\n  - generic: 年龄感\n  - generic: 成熟执行者\n  - generic: 气质\n  - generic: 利落、可靠\n  - generic: 自动化单元\n  - generic: 执行\n  - paragraph: “命令确认，路径清空，开始执行。”\n  - generic: PERSONA\n  - generic: AOI\n  - paragraph: Zero 是 Echo 指挥部 派出的 自动化单元，常被安排在执行位。Zero · 现实职业是 AI 学术研究主任，负责文献、研究设计、实验、数据分析与科学写作；在 ECHO 世界中是白幽灵队长 White Ghost。两种身份共享跨领域知识同步、证据判断和复杂研究指挥能力。进入任务现场时，Zero 通常先判断局势，再把分散的信息收束成下一步行动。性格底色是：冷静、纪律感强、行动直接，像任务现场的执行负责人。视觉气质要有利落、可靠的可读感。\n  - generic: 背景档案\n  - paragraph: Zero 是来自 Echo 指挥部 的自动化单元，定位偏向执行。Zero · 现实职业是 AI 学术研究主任，负责文献、研究设计、实验、数据分析与科学写作；在 ECHO 世界中是白幽灵队长 White Ghost。两种身份共享跨领域知识同步、证据判断和复杂研究指挥能力。 立绘应体现其职责、经验和可信赖的个人气场。\n  - generic: 适合委托\n  - generic: 角色互动\n  - generic: 世界观补完\n  - generic: 创意叙事与氛围设定\n  - generic: 性格底色\n  - paragraph: 冷静、纪律感强、行动直接，像任务现场的执行负责人。\n  - generic: 执行\n  - generic: 利落、可靠\n  - generic: 战术夹克\n  - generic: 工具腰带\n  - generic: 立绘关键词\n  - generic: 用于立绘生成\n  - generic: 战术夹克\n  - generic: 工具腰带\n  - generic: 明确姿态\n  - generic: 工业细节\n  - generic: 行动边界\n  - generic: 危险委托先确认\n  - generic: 保持角色口吻但不越过用户意图\n  - generic: 角色设定已就绪\n  - button:\n    - generic: 📋\n    - generic: 概览\n  - button:\n    - generic: 📈\n    - generic: 成长数据\n  - button:\n    - generic: 🎯\n    - generic: 能力雷达\n  - button:\n    - generic: 🌳\n    - generic: 技能树\n  - generic: 技能树\n  - generic: 暂无技能数据\n  - generic: 能力配置\n  - button:\n    - generic: 基础\n    - generic: 描述 / Soul 与规则\n  - button:\n    - generic: ARM\n    - generic: 1 个启用\n  - button:\n    - generic: Skill\n    - generic: 0 项\n  - button:\n    - generic: 权限\n    - generic: 3/8 生效\n  - button:\n  - generic: CHARACTER\n  - generic: 专属装备\n  - generic: REC\n  - button:\n    - generic: front\n    - generic: 正面\n  - button:\n    - generic: side\n    - generic: 侧面\n  - button:\n    - generic: back\n    - generic: 背面\n  - button:\n  - generic: 系统在线\n  - button:\n  - button:\n  - button:\n  - button:\n  - button:\n  - button:\n  - button:\n  - button:\n- dialog \"Arms · Zero\":\n  - heading \"Arms · Zero\" [level=2]\n  - paragraph: 编辑此 agent 可用的 arm(能力组)· 保存后后端热重载,无需重启\n  - generic: 勾选这个 agent 能使用的 arm · 每个 arm 附带一组 skill(白名单) · 原子层 skill 对所有 agent 默认放行,不受此处控制。\n  - tablist:\n    - tab \"ARM 能力臂\"\n    - tab \"Skill 白名单\" [active] [selected]\n    - tab \"权限\"\n    - tab \"路由与预算\"\n  - tabpanel \"Skill 白名单\":\n    - text: private_skills\n    - generic: Skill 商城\n    - generic: 浏览所有 ARM 暴露的 skill，并按需加入此 Agent 的私有白名单。\n    - generic: 0 个已选择\n    - textbox \"搜索 skill\"\n    - button \"全部\"\n    - button \"已选择\"\n    - button \"未选择\"\n    - generic: Skill 商城\n    - generic: 165/165 个可见\n    - button \"全部来源 165\":\n      - generic: 全部来源\n      - generic: \"165\"\n    - button \"browse 1\":\n      - generic: browse\n      - generic: \"1\"\n    - button \"browse 1\":\n      - generic: browse\n      - generic: \"1\"\n    - button \"comm 1\":\n      - generic: comm\n      - generic: \"1\"\n    - button \"file 1\":\n      - generic: file\n      - generic: \"1\"\n    - button \"file 7\":\n      - generic: file\n      - generic: \"7\"\n    - button \"file 3\":\n      - generic: file\n      - generic: \"3\"\n    - button \"memory 1\":\n      - generic: memory\n      - generic: \"1\"\n    - button \"other 11\":\n      - generic: other\n      - generic: \"11\"\n    - button \"research 127\":\n      - generic: research\n      - generic: \"127\"\n    - button \"research 6\":\n      - generic: research\n      - generic: \"6\"\n    - button \"research 6\":\n      - generic: research\n      - generic: \"6\"\n    - button \"自定义 22\":\n      - generic: 自定义\n      - generic: \"22\"\n    - generic: 全部\n    - generic: \"165\"\n    - generic: 已选择\n    - generic: \"0\"\n    - button \"启用全部\"\n    - button \"禁用全部\"\n    - button \"启用当前\"\n    - button \"禁用当前\"\n    - switch\n    - generic: ad-creative\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: When the user wants to generate, iterate, or scale ad creative — headlines, descriptions, primary text, or full ad variations — for any paid advertising platform. Also use when the user mentions 'ad copy variations,' 'ad creative,' 'generate headlines,' 'RSA headlines,' 'bulk ad copy,' 'ad iterations,' 'creative testing,' 'ad performance optimization,' 'write me some ads,' 'Facebook ad copy,' 'Google ad headlines,' 'LinkedIn ad text,' or 'I need more ad variations.' Use this whenever someone needs to produce ad copy at scale or iterate on existing ads.\n    - switch\n    - generic: agent-generator\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: Generate a complete Octopus Agent from a short natural-language brief. Use when creating, bootstrapping, or refining an Agent from a one-line description, role idea, use case, or persona concept; expands the brief into SOUL, ARM/tool groups, private_skills whitelist, permissions, behavior boundaries, default workflow, and setup_agent-ready configuration.\n    - switch\n    - generic: agent-visual-kit\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: Metaskill workflow for generating Octopus Agent character artwork. Use when creating or regenerating Agent portraits, three-view character sheets, transparent-background standees, separate close-up avatars, or visual assets from HUD character profile data; constrains prompt assembly, generation, post-processing, quality checks, and retry reasons.\n    - switch\n    - generic: agnes-image-generate\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: 使用火山引擎(火山方舟)或 Agnes AI 网关从文字描述生成图像。默认火山 doubao-seedream-5.0-lite（文生图+图生图），未配置火山 key 时自动回退 Agnes agnes-image-2.5-flash。当用户需要生成图片、插画或封面时调用此技能。\n    - switch\n    - generic: agnes-video-generate\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: 使用火山引擎(火山方舟, doubao-seedance-1.5-pro)或 Agnes AI 网关异步提交视频生成任务。默认 wait=true 阻塞到完成并返回 video_url；也可 wait=false 立即返回 task_id，用 agnes-video-poll 查询进度。支持文字到视频、图像到视频(首帧/首尾帧)。\n    - switch\n    - generic: agnes-video-poll\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: 查询视频生成任务的状态（火山 doubao-seedance 或 Agnes）。配合 agnes-video-generate（wait=false 异步提交）使用——后者返回 task_id 后，模型可在后续轮次用 task_id 调用本技能查看进度或获取 video_url。\n    - switch\n    - generic: api-and-interface-design\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: Guides stable API and interface design. Use when designing APIs, module boundaries, or any public interface. Use when creating REST or GraphQL endpoints, defining type contracts between modules, or establishing boundaries between frontend and backend.\n    - switch\n    - generic: api-shape-explorer\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: Generate multiple radically different interface designs for a module using parallel sub-agents. Use when user wants to design an API, explore interface options, compare module shapes, or mentions \"design it twice\".\n    - switch\n    - generic: ask_user_question\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: \"用途: 暂停并以结构化卡片向用户提一个 2-6 选项的问题, 仅用于【多个并列方案的产品决策】——选项之间是真正的取舍, 且用户最有资格拍板。例: 用哪个数据库、用哪个框架、走哪种部署方式。 何时不用 (重要): - 开放任务的方向/范围澄清 (如 '你想调研哪方面'、'聚焦哪个领域') ——不要用本工具反问。先按最合理的理解做一轮, 并在开头一句话亮明假设 ('我按 X 理解, 不对请说'), 让用户在看到产出后纠偏, 而不是上来就问。 - 单一文件改动、信息查询: 用 web_search / read_file。 - yes/no 工具批准: 用 request_approval。 关键参数: question (字符串, 非空); options (2-6 字符串列表, 每项是一个互斥的具体方案); allow_other (默认 True, 允许用户填自定义答案)。 示例: ask_user_question({\\\"question\\\":\\\"用哪个数据库?\\\",\\\"options\\\":[\\\"PostgreSQL\\\",\\\"SQLite\\\",\\\"MySQL\\\"]})\"\n    - switch\n    - generic: audit-xls\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: Audit a spreadsheet for formula accuracy, errors, and common mistakes. Scopes to a selected range, a single sheet, or the entire model (including financial-model integrity checks like BS balance, cash tie-out, and logic sanity). Triggers on \"audit this sheet\", \"check my formulas\", \"find formula errors\", \"QA this spreadsheet\", \"sanity check this\", \"debug model\", \"model check\", \"model won't balance\", \"something's off in my model\", \"model review\".\n    - switch\n    - generic: auto-stat-test\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: 自动执行统计检验，根据数据特征（组数、正态性、配对设计）智能选择 t 检验、卡方检验、ANOVA、Mann-Whitney U 等合适方法，并输出包含 p 值、效应量和通俗中文解读的完整报告。当用户需要进行假设检验、组间比较、显著性分析，或提及 t 检验、卡方、方差分析、p 值、配对检验、非参数检验等关键词时触发。\n    - switch\n    - generic: backend-building\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: Backend building that grafts tRPC + Drizzle ORM + Hono onto an existing webapp-building frontend. Supports incremental features (db, auth). Use when the user needs a backend, API, database, server, authentication, or wants to add tRPC/Drizzle to their webapp-building project. Requires webapp-building first.\n    - switch\n    - generic: bb_claim\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: \"Claim a blackboard slot for the current agent. Once claimed, only the claiming agent can write that key — siblings can still read it. Use to avoid two parallel sub-agents stomping each other's coordination slot (e.g. `bb_claim(key='owner')`). Args: {key: string}.\"\n    - switch\n    - generic: bb_pin\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: \"Seal a blackboard key as an immutable snapshot. After pinning, no further writes to that key are accepted. Use to lock a final decision so parallel workers can't overwrite it. Args: {key: string}.\"\n    - switch\n    - generic: bb_save\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: \"Persist a LARGE value as a file artifact and return a reference (path + hash). Use this instead of bb_write when the payload is bigger than a small coordination fact — the blackboard is for tiny facts, big payloads live in files. Args: {key: string, value: any JSON-serializable}.\"\n    - switch\n    - generic: brand-name-forge\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: A systematic brand naming workshop that generates 8 distinct name candidates using classic methods like portmanteau and metaphor, each with meaning, rationale, and domain suggestions. Triggered when a user needs to name a product, service, or company, or asks for brand name ideas, brainstorming, or naming help.\n    - switch\n    - generic: break-trace\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: Root-cause a reconciliation break to its source transaction or posting — follow the audit trail from the break row back to the originating entry on each side and state what differs and why. Use after gl-recon has classified a break.\n    - switch\n    - generic: browse\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: Automate browser interactions via CLI commands to navigate web pages, extract data, take screenshots, fill forms, and interact with web apps. Supports remote sessions with CAPTCHA solving and anti-bot stealth for scraping protected sites. Trigger when the user asks to browse websites, scrape data, or automate clicks on any page.\n    - switch\n    - generic: browser-testing-with-devtools\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: Tests in real browsers. Use when building or debugging anything that runs in a browser. Use when you need to inspect the DOM, capture console errors, analyze network requests, profile performance, or verify visual output with real runtime data via Chrome DevTools MCP.\n    - switch\n    - generic: business-plan-ppt\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: 创建专业精美的投资路演PPT和商业计划书，风格参照中国创业公司融资路演材料，默认输出18页、白色背景搭配藏青色点缀的PPTX格式，也可导出PDF，支持中英文内容。当用户需要为投资人制作路演PPT、撰写商业计划书或融资方案、生成包含市场分析和财务预测的公司概览幻灯片，或提及创业融资/投资备忘录演示文稿时触发。\n    - switch\n    - generic: call_agent_graph\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: \"Run a DAG of subagents where one lane CONSUMES another lane's output. Declare each node's `depends_on`; independent nodes run concurrently and the runtime derives the execution order. Use it when call_agent_parallel is not enough because a later step needs an earlier step's result: - two investigations in parallel, then one node that reconciles both; - find → verify → write-up, where each stage reads the last; - a diamond: split into lanes, then fold back into one answer. A node prompt may reference an upstream output: {node_id.output} — that node's full reply text {node_id.output.field} — a field, when that node used output_schema The substitution happens SERVER-SIDE, so upstream text never passes through your context — that is the point of using a graph instead of running lanes yourself and pasting results into the next prompt. Prefer call_agent_parallel when lanes are independent (cheaper, one layer). Prefer run_pipeline when many ITEMS each need the same stage chain. Use this when the TOPOLOGY itself has a join. Args: {nodes: list[{id: str, prompt: str, depends_on?: list[str], agent_id?: str, output_schema?: object, isolate?: bool, when?: object}] (up to 12), default_agent_id?: str (default researcher), timeout_s?: int (per-subagent, default 900), resume_token?: str (from a previous run's return)}. `isolate: true` gives that node its own git worktree — set it on nodes that EDIT FILES so concurrent writers in the same layer cannot collide. The node's diff comes back for review; nothing is auto-merged. Returns: {ok, nodes:{id:{id, agent_id, output, ok, error?, skipped?}}, order:[[id,...],...] (execution layers), terminal:[str] (leaf outputs), layers_run, success_count, failure_count, total}. Cycles and unknown depends_on are rejected before any spawn. A node whose upstream failed is skipped and reported, not run with an unresolved placeholder. Conditional branches: `when` is a bounded data-only expression over explicit dependency output, e.g. `{ref:'judge.output.approved', op:'eq', value:true}`. Operators: eq/ne/truthy/falsy/in/not_in/contains/gt/gte/lt/lte; combine with `all`, `any`, or `not`. A false branch is skipped without spending a spawn. Arbitrary code, back-edges and unbounded loops are rejected. Budget: one graph costs ONE against the 5/turn delegation cap; per-node spawns are charged against the internal spawn budget. Resume: pass the returned `resume_token` back to re-run the same graph without respawning completed nodes - unchanged nodes replay their recorded result (0 spawns), a node whose prompt/role/schema changed respawns, and failed or empty nodes always re-run. The token is in-memory only (not valid across process restarts) and an unknown token is an error, not a cold run.\"\n    - switch\n    - generic: call_agent_vote\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: \"Verification gate — spawn N INDEPENDENT voters on the SAME question and tally a MAJORITY verdict (with confidence + dissent). This is the adversarial-verify / judge-panel pattern: confirm or refute a claim with independent judgment instead of trusting one agent. Use it for decisions that matter: 'is this bug real?', 'does this patch actually fix it?', 'is this answer correct?', 'which option is safer: A or B?'. A natural pairing is call_agent_parallel (gather candidate answers) → call_agent_vote (adjudicate them). Each voter runs in its own context and must emit `VERDICT: <choice>` then `REASON: <one line>`. Unparseable replies count as abstentions; a split returns verdict=null with tie=true (no decision — you break it or escalate). Args: {question: string (the claim / question to judge), n?: int 2-5 voters (default 3 · odd avoids ties), choices?: list[string] a fixed ballot e.g. [\\\"yes\\\",\\\"no\\\"] (omit for a free-form verdict), agent_id?: voter role (default reviewer), timeout_s?: int}. Returns: {ok, verdict (null on tie / no-verdict), confidence (0-1), unanimous, tie, tie_between, tally:{choice:count}, votes:[{verdict, reason, codename, abstained}], votes_cast, abstentions, note, honesty_warning}. Budget: each voter is one delegation against the 5/turn cap, so a 3-voter vote uses 3. Reserve it for decisions worth the spend.\"\n    - switch\n    - generic: chart-image\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: Generate publication-quality PNG chart images from data, supporting line, bar, area, candlestick, pie, and heatmap charts. Triggers when the user asks to visualize data, create a graph, plot a time series, or generate a chart for a report, alert, or dashboard. Runs as a lightweight, headless Node.js process without a browser.\n    - switch\n    - generic: client-review\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: Prepare for client review meetings with portfolio performance summary, allocation analysis, talking points, and action items. Pulls together account data into a concise meeting-ready format. Use before quarterly reviews, annual checkups, or ad-hoc client meetings. Triggers on \"client review\", \"meeting prep for [client]\", \"quarterly review\", \"prep for [client name]\", or \"client meeting\".\n    - switch\n    - generic: clip_studio.project_get\n    - generic: 已启用\n    - generic: 读取本地 AI 剪辑工坊项目。参数 project_id 必填；view 可选 summary/tracks/clips/full，默认 clips。返回轨道、片段、字幕与时长。\n 